  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "New benchmarks and ablations test molecular ML under controlled splits, baselines and multi-stage filters, showing that representation choice and training gains are conditional.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is controlled evaluation of molecular and protein ML, with attention on benchmark design, baselines and stage-wise filtering rather than architecture. PeptSol supplies 1388 curated protected-peptide solubility measurements with chemistry-aware splits for seven frozen encoders. Ark-ADMET reports that endpoint-specific representation and hyperparameter selection under the TDC protocol matches or beats leaderboard scores on 7 of 21 endpoints. The DiffDock fixed-budget study found no gain from focused or mixed torsional supervision. HEDGEHOG shows attrition among 22 generators on KRAS G12D that standard metrics miss. The antibody-agent paper compares an agentic optimizer with a Bayesian optimization baseline. Several other items, including RangeFinder, ProteoCraft, FoldAbS and the olfactory contrastive model, are method papers rather than benchmarks.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
